# Testing a PRD

A PRD has tests too. They are structural and they run on every edit.
`check_prd.py` covers the mechanical checks. `/pm-validate` covers judgment.

## 1. Every story is INVEST

Fill the INVEST Check table in each story file. Each row is Yes plus one line of evidence.

| Letter | Fails when |
|---|---|
| Independent | It needs another story in the same sprint to ship |
| Negotiable | It prescribes a UI widget or an implementation |
| Valuable | No named user gets a visible change |
| Estimable | The team needs a spike before sizing it |
| Small | Size is larger than L, or it has more than 5 AC |
| Testable | Any AC has no observable Then |

The story sentence is one line: `As a <user>, I want <capability> so that <outcome>.`
Missing "I want" or "so that" is a defect. The `invest-validator` hook warns on it.

## 2. Every AC is Given/When/Then

```markdown
- **Given** <starting state with concrete values>
- **When** <one user action or one system event>
- **Then** <one observable outcome>
```

- At least one AC per story. Number them `AC1`, `AC2`.
- Use real values: "a $400 limit and $360 spent", not "a limit and some spending".
- "Gracefully", "quickly", "user-friendly" are banned in a Then. Say what the user sees.

## 3. Every NFR is measurable

Each NFR has a number, a percentile, a time window or a named standard.

| Category | Pass | Fail |
|---|---|---|
| Performance | p95 < 2 s from event to alert | "fast" |
| Security | data class + auth model named | "secure" |
| Privacy | retention days + consent model | absent |
| Accessibility | WCAG 2.2 AA | "accessible" |
| Internationalization | locales + currency format listed | absent |
| Observability | metric names + alert threshold | "add monitoring later" |

## 4. Traceability is complete

- Every story names one epic (`**Epic:** E1`) and one goal (`**Goal:** G1`).
- The epic exists in the PRD Epics table and points at the same goal.
- Every goal has at least one epic. Every epic has at least one story.
- Every story file appears in the PRD User Stories index.

## 5. Edge cases are named

List edge cases as named scenarios, each with the story that handles it.
"Handle errors" is not an edge case.

## Running the tests

```bash
npx markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1
python3 scripts/check_prd.py .            # skeleton and draft phases
python3 scripts/check_prd.py . --strict   # before /pm-validate and /pm-decompose
```

Exit code 0 means pass. Fix every reported line before moving phase.
